WEBVTT

00:06.400 --> 00:09.517
- Wake up, wake up, wake up.
- I'm sorry, Mom. I love you.

00:10.520 --> 00:12.078
- What?
- What?

00:12.880 --> 00:14.518
There's something you gotta see.

00:16.160 --> 00:18.435
It has to be better than my dream.

00:20.200 --> 00:23.192
- Wake up, wake up, wake up.
- It's Dad's magazine.

00:23.960 --> 00:25.393
- What?
- What?

00:25.880 --> 00:27.791
There's something you gotta see.

00:28.600 --> 00:31.592
I was already seeing everything
I needed to see.

00:33.360 --> 00:34.349
What's going on?

00:34.520 --> 00:36.875
Remember how I recorded
those kids' songs months ago?

00:37.040 --> 00:38.519
Yeah, they sucked.

00:39.200 --> 00:41.509
Of course they sucked,
they're kids' songs.

00:42.320 --> 00:44.993
The CD's coming out,
and the first commercial's about to air.

00:45.160 --> 00:46.195
At 5 in the morning?

00:46.360 --> 00:48.191
That's when moms
with little kids are up.

00:48.360 --> 00:50.430
Oh, &lt;i>Becker's&lt;/i> over. I'm up next.

00:50.840 --> 00:51.989
&lt;i>Who loves kids?&lt;/i>

00:52.160 --> 00:54.469
&lt;i>Charlie Waffles.&lt;/i>

00:55.760 --> 00:57.079
&lt;i>Who cut the cheese?&lt;/i>

00:57.440 --> 00:58.839
&lt;i>Who cut the cheese?&lt;/i>

00:59.160 --> 01:02.197
&lt;i>I ask you please&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Did you cut the cheese?&lt;/i>

01:02.640 --> 01:04.915
&lt;i>That's right. Charlie Waffles.&lt;/i>

01:05.080 --> 01:08.072
&lt;i>And now,&lt;/i>
&lt;i>you can get his greatest hits on one CD.&lt;/i>

01:08.680 --> 01:10.671
- Charlie Waffles?
- My idea.

01:11.080 --> 01:13.992
- Kids love waffles.
- That's true.

01:14.400 --> 01:17.233
&lt;i>Yes, you'll get all the melodies&lt;/i>
&lt;i>that made Charlie Waffles...&lt;/i>

01:17.400 --> 01:18.799
&lt;i>... the king of kids ' songs.&lt;/i>

01:18.960 --> 01:24.114
&lt;i>"Kiss My Owie," "Rush to Flush,"&lt;/i>
&lt;i>and of course, "Don 't Shake the Baby."&lt;/i>

01:24.280 --> 01:26.999
&lt;i>He's a little boy&lt;/i>
&lt;i>He is not a toy&lt;/i>

01:27.160 --> 01:30.516
&lt;i>Don 't shake, shake, shake the baby&lt;/i>

01:30.960 --> 01:33.952
&lt;i>She's our little pearl&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Our darling girl&lt;/i>

01:34.120 --> 01:37.556
&lt;i>Don 't shake, shake, shake the baby&lt;/i>

01:39.000 --> 01:40.991
When did you become
the king of kids' songs?

01:41.400 --> 01:43.630
When did you become
the Federal Trade Commission?

01:44.400 --> 01:47.756
&lt;i>Grandma may smell funny&lt;/i>
&lt;i>But hug her anyway&lt;/i>

01:47.920 --> 01:51.230
&lt;i>Accept her stinky kisses&lt;/i>
&lt;i>And then go out and play&lt;/i>

01:51.720 --> 01:55.156
&lt;i>But she's got all the money&lt;/i>
&lt;i>So you might just want to stay&lt;/i>

01:55.320 --> 01:57.231
&lt;i>Oh, Grandma may smell funny...&lt;/i>

01:57.400 --> 01:58.833
&lt;i>But wait, there's more.&lt;/i>

01:59.000 --> 02:00.513
&lt;i>With this special TV offer...&lt;/i>

02:00.680 --> 02:04.514
&lt;i>... you'll also receive&lt;/i>
&lt;i>this never-before-released bonus track.&lt;/i>

02:04.680 --> 02:08.036
&lt;i>I drink from a sippy cup&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Sippy cup, sippy cup&lt;/i>

02:08.200 --> 02:11.590
&lt;i>I drink from a sippy cup&lt;/i>
&lt;i>'Cause I'm a big kid now&lt;/i>

02:12.080 --> 02:13.672
&lt;i>Bye-bye, boobies&lt;/i>

02:13.840 --> 02:15.068
&lt;i>Bye-bye, boobies&lt;/i>

02:15.480 --> 02:18.677
&lt;i>Bye-bye, boobies&lt;/i>
&lt;i>'Cause I'm a big kid now&lt;/i>

02:18.840 --> 02:23.755
&lt;i>Call now and you'll also receive a bonus&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Charlie Waffles scratch-and-sniff poster.&lt;/i>

02:23.920 --> 02:26.354
&lt;i>It smells just like maple syrup.&lt;/i>

02:26.520 --> 02:28.750
What, they couldn't make it
smell like bourbon?

02:28.920 --> 02:32.879
&lt;i>Operators are standing by.&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Give your child the gift of music.&lt;/i>

02:33.040 --> 02:35.873
- &lt;i>Who loves kids?&lt;/i>
- &lt;i>Charlie Waffles.&lt;/i>

02:36.040 --> 02:37.632
&lt;i>Right.&lt;/i>

02:39.400 --> 02:41.152
That's it. What do you think?

02:43.680 --> 02:45.591
I'm going back to bed.

02:46.520 --> 02:50.149
- What about you?
- You couldn't have TiVo'd this?

02:50.600 --> 02:54.718
Hey, Charlie Waffles may love kids,
but he's getting pretty sick of you.

02:56.600 --> 02:58.750
Oh, boy, &lt;i>Dharma and Greg.&lt;/i>

03:29.400 --> 03:32.278
I still don't understand why
you wanted to come shopping with me.

03:32.440 --> 03:35.955
- I told you. I gotta pick up something.
- You could have just put it on the list.

03:36.120 --> 03:38.839
Hey, maybe I just wanna
hang out with my brother.

03:39.000 --> 03:42.709
- Really? Oh, well, that's a very nice...
- Get away, get away, get away.

03:45.080 --> 03:46.877
Of course.

03:55.360 --> 03:56.395
Excuse me.

03:56.560 --> 03:58.551
Do you know
where the chewable vitamins are?

03:59.120 --> 04:01.236
Oh, I think they're...

04:02.000 --> 04:03.513
Oh, my God, you're him.

04:04.000 --> 04:06.070
- I'm sorry?
- You're Charlie Waffles, right?

04:07.120 --> 04:09.873
- You caught me.
- My daughter just loves your songs.

04:10.040 --> 04:13.715
Oh, gee, you don't know
how that fills my heart.

04:14.120 --> 04:16.873
There's about to be
a vomit spill on Aisle 3.

04:17.400 --> 04:19.277
- How old is your little girl?
- Five.

04:19.440 --> 04:22.273
No way. What, did you have her
when you were 12?

04:22.440 --> 04:24.192
- Oh, you're sweet.
- I know.

04:24.360 --> 04:27.352
Hey, she's not gonna believe I met you.
Can I take a picture of you?

04:27.520 --> 04:29.875
- Better still, let's take one together.
- Oh, okay.

04:30.040 --> 04:31.951
Excuse me, sir.
Would you take our picture?

04:34.880 --> 04:36.108
Sir?

04:36.880 --> 04:38.916
Oh, yeah, yeah. Sure.

04:41.520 --> 04:42.999
Say "waffles."

04:43.160 --> 04:44.593
- Waffles.
- Waffles.

04:46.480 --> 04:48.471
- Thanks, pal.
- Thank you.

04:48.640 --> 04:50.039
Don't let your husband see that.

04:50.200 --> 04:52.430
He might get the wrong idea
about Charlie Waffles.

04:52.600 --> 04:55.319
- Oh, there is no husband.
- No kidding?

04:55.480 --> 04:57.914
Oh, my God.

04:58.840 --> 05:01.832
Jodie is gonna love this.
I'm gonna save it for her birthday.

05:02.000 --> 05:03.149
Her birthday's coming up?

05:03.320 --> 05:06.357
- This weekend, she'll be 6.
- Oh, what a magical age.

05:06.920 --> 05:11.550
Tell you what. How would Jodie like
a free Charlie Waffles birthday concert?

05:12.240 --> 05:13.229
You would do that?

05:13.960 --> 05:14.995
Who loves kids?

05:15.640 --> 05:17.073
Charlie Waffles.

05:17.920 --> 05:20.639
Right. Call me.

05:22.840 --> 05:25.991
Look, it's got a little waffle on it.
How adorable.

05:28.040 --> 05:30.679
I told you I had to pick something up.

05:33.280 --> 05:36.511
&lt;i>Grandma may smell funny&lt;/i>
&lt;i>But hug her anyway&lt;/i>

05:36.880 --> 05:40.316
&lt;i>Accept her stinky kisses&lt;/i>
&lt;i>And then go out and play&lt;/i>

05:40.600 --> 05:43.990
&lt;i>But she's got all the money&lt;/i>
&lt;i>So you might just want to stay&lt;/i>

05:44.160 --> 05:47.994
&lt;i>Oh, Grandma may smell funny&lt;/i>
&lt;i>But hug her anyway&lt;/i>

05:48.360 --> 05:51.432
&lt;i>Hug her anyway&lt;/i>
&lt;i>So hug her anyway&lt;/i>

05:51.600 --> 05:53.591
&lt;i>Sing&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Hug her anyway&lt;/i>

05:54.760 --> 05:55.795
Pretty catchy, huh?

05:56.400 --> 05:58.391
So is gonorrhea.

05:59.280 --> 06:01.271
Drinking from the well of bitterness,
are we?

06:01.720 --> 06:04.154
I just don't understand
what kind of spiteful god...

06:04.320 --> 06:06.675
...could allow my drunken
whoremonger of a brother...

06:06.840 --> 06:08.637
...to become a children's singing star...

06:08.800 --> 06:11.473
...while I toil away
in poverty-stricken anonymity.

06:11.880 --> 06:15.316
You wanna talk to me about toiling away
in poverty-stricken anonymity?

06:16.240 --> 06:19.949
No. Sorry.
I'm sure you've got it worse than I do.

06:20.120 --> 06:22.839
Whoa, whoa, I wouldn't go that far.

06:24.480 --> 06:25.708
What I'm trying to say is...

06:25.880 --> 06:28.269
...there's another way to look at this.
- What's that?

06:28.440 --> 06:30.078
We're all in this together.

06:30.240 --> 06:33.630
Your brother's success is our success.
His home is our home.

06:33.800 --> 06:36.917
And most importantly, when
he's got a load on, his car is my car.

06:40.400 --> 06:42.356
Hey, Berta, guess what.

06:42.840 --> 06:46.355
- I got another big royalty check.
- Oh, hey, good for you.

06:46.760 --> 06:50.275
- Why don't you celebrate with a drink?
- Well, I think I will.

06:51.960 --> 06:54.269
- Hey, Alan, guess what.
- Yeah, I heard.

06:54.440 --> 06:55.839
Another big check.

06:58.800 --> 07:01.109
You know what's a great place
to pick up single moms?

07:01.280 --> 07:04.272
- The parking lot of Chuck E. Cheese.
- You didn't.

07:04.440 --> 07:07.159
And not just moms. Nannies, aunts...

07:07.320 --> 07:09.914
...and a couple of very doable grandmas.

07:12.000 --> 07:13.149
Do you have any shame?

07:14.040 --> 07:15.792
No, why?

07:19.640 --> 07:21.073
Hello?

07:21.880 --> 07:22.915
Hang on.

07:24.840 --> 07:26.512
Who loves kids?

07:26.680 --> 07:28.830
Oh, hey, Artie.
Just got the check. Thanks.

07:29.000 --> 07:30.479
What's up?

07:31.440 --> 07:34.034
Sure, I'll sign some CDs. Where?

07:34.360 --> 07:37.079
They got bookstores just for kids?
Who knew?

07:37.480 --> 07:39.550
Everyone but you.

07:39.720 --> 07:42.359
Okay, I'll be there. Thanks a lot.

07:42.520 --> 07:44.476
- Hey, Alan, guess what.
- There is no God?

07:44.640 --> 07:49.316
Oh, on the contrary,
there is a God, and he love me long time.

07:53.920 --> 07:57.276
&lt;i>Who barfed in the fishbowl?&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Who could it be?&lt;/i>

07:57.720 --> 08:01.235
&lt;i>Who barfed in the fishbowl?&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Oh, wait, it's me&lt;/i>

08:01.400 --> 08:04.915
&lt;i>Fish food, fish food&lt;/i>
&lt;i>I made some fish food&lt;/i>

08:05.080 --> 08:08.914
&lt;i>Fish food, fish food&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Mommy, come and see&lt;/i>

08:14.840 --> 08:17.798
Love, Charlie Waffles.

08:17.960 --> 08:18.995
There you go, Dakota.

08:19.440 --> 08:22.512
- What do we say to Mr. Waffles?
- Thank you, Mr. Waffles.

08:22.680 --> 08:25.399
No, thank you, sweetheart.
And thank you, Mommy.

08:25.560 --> 08:28.518
So tell me, is there a Mrs. Waffles?

08:28.920 --> 08:32.356
- Sadly, no.
- Well, maybe this will cheer you up.

08:33.920 --> 08:35.399
Come on, honey.

08:35.880 --> 08:37.996
Oh, it do indeed.

08:38.520 --> 08:39.635
This guy's a phenomenon.

08:39.800 --> 08:42.837
The label's moved 100,000 units
in less than two weeks.

08:43.000 --> 08:46.276
The Wiggles can kiss my pasty,
white tushy.

08:47.200 --> 08:48.269
I'm sorry, who are you?

08:48.920 --> 08:52.356
Oh, I'm Artie Pliskin. President
and CEO of Fluffy Bunny Records.

08:52.520 --> 08:54.829
- And you are?
- Alan, Charlie's brother.

08:55.000 --> 08:56.752
Oh, you're the sponge. It's a pleasure.

08:59.600 --> 09:00.749
Same here.

09:02.680 --> 09:05.478
- Do you believe in God, Artie?
- I'll tell you what I believe in.

09:05.640 --> 09:09.553
Regular prostate exams, full-release
massage and Charlie freaking Waffles.

09:14.160 --> 09:17.277
Okay, kids, Charlie Waffles
needs to take a little potty break...

09:17.440 --> 09:19.237
...but he'll be right back.

09:19.400 --> 09:22.119
In the meantime,
why don't you all sing along?

09:23.400 --> 09:25.118
&lt;i>It's potty time&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Can 't hold it&lt;/i>

09:25.560 --> 09:27.471
&lt;i>Can 't hold it&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Can 't hold it&lt;/i>

09:28.280 --> 09:30.350
Here, put this
in the "Mommy and Me" pile.

09:31.440 --> 09:32.589
I'll be right back.

09:32.760 --> 09:35.797
This is nothing compared to the concert
he's gonna give next weekend.

09:35.960 --> 09:37.552
- Concert?
- Concert?

09:37.720 --> 09:39.472
Twelve-hundred
screaming kids and moms...

09:39.640 --> 09:41.949
...all dying to hear
Charlie Waffles sing in person.

09:42.800 --> 09:43.789
Twelve-hundred?

09:44.440 --> 09:45.873
At 50 bucks a pop.

09:46.040 --> 09:50.670
Wait, wait a minute. He's gonna
make $60,000 off one concert?

09:50.840 --> 09:53.718
Yeah. Good time to be a sponge, huh?

09:56.360 --> 09:57.554
I'm not doing any concerts.

09:58.160 --> 10:01.391
- Why not?
- Because I'm not. Case closed.

10:01.920 --> 10:03.273
What's up with him?

10:03.440 --> 10:07.433
It would appear he's displeased with the
latest gold nugget to fall out of his ass.

10:07.600 --> 10:08.589
Yeah, well, trust me.

10:09.040 --> 10:13.318
The gold's gonna keep coming,
even if I have to get it myself.

10:15.320 --> 10:16.878
&lt;i>Potty&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Potty&lt;/i>

10:22.800 --> 10:24.279
So?

10:25.040 --> 10:27.076
Waffle for your thoughts?

10:27.360 --> 10:29.237
- Leave me alone.
- I don't understand.

10:29.400 --> 10:32.756
I would think a sold-out concert
would be good news for Charlie Waffles.

10:32.920 --> 10:36.708
- Yeah, well, it's not.
- Because?

10:37.360 --> 10:39.874
You ever wonder
why I never played in a band?

10:40.040 --> 10:42.076
I just figured you were
getting laid so much...

10:42.240 --> 10:44.674
...being in a rock band
would seem redundant.

10:44.840 --> 10:46.717
That's not the reason.

10:46.880 --> 10:48.996
Although I did do better
than most bass players.

10:49.160 --> 10:50.912
Okay, then what is the reason?

10:52.400 --> 10:55.278
- I have stage fright.
- You have stage fright?

10:55.440 --> 10:59.115
Severe, debilitating,
wet-your-pants stage fright.

11:04.360 --> 11:05.634
I don't understand.

11:07.360 --> 11:08.588
I've seen you perform.

11:09.080 --> 11:11.548
Well, sure, in the living room
for a couple of people.

11:11.720 --> 11:15.793
But on a stage with lights,
in front of a crowd paying to see me...

11:17.080 --> 11:19.150
Do you literally pee your pants?

11:20.160 --> 11:21.434
What difference does it make?

11:21.600 --> 11:24.114
I'm just saying your audience
is composed of bed wetters.

11:24.280 --> 11:27.397
They might get a kick out of
seeing you soil yourself.

11:27.920 --> 11:30.036
- And you think that'd be funny?
- No, I wouldn't.

11:30.200 --> 11:32.236
But I'm not your audience.

11:38.320 --> 11:39.799
Hello?

11:40.680 --> 11:42.955
I don't know what to tell you, Artie.
I can't do it.

11:43.480 --> 11:46.438
- I don't need a reason why.
- Just tell him the truth.

11:47.400 --> 11:50.597
It's show business, Alan,
you don't tell people the truth.

11:51.680 --> 11:54.274
Look, I'll make the CDs,
I'll shoot the commercials...

11:54.440 --> 11:57.193
...I'll even do the bookstores.
Just no concerts.

11:58.640 --> 12:01.677
Hey, I don't have to do anything.

12:02.120 --> 12:03.872
Oh, yeah?
What are you gonna do, sue me?

12:05.400 --> 12:06.833
Really?

12:09.440 --> 12:11.715
- Can he sue me?
- Did you sign a contract?

12:12.200 --> 12:13.713
What time is the concert?

12:15.560 --> 12:17.471
Okay, see you Saturday night.

12:17.640 --> 12:20.393
Wait, wait, wait. Eleven a. M?

12:20.560 --> 12:23.472
Who goes to concerts at 11 a. M?

12:24.120 --> 12:25.917
Oh, yeah.

12:27.080 --> 12:29.275
Stupid kids.

12:32.600 --> 12:34.033
&lt;i>It's quarter to 1

12:34.200 --> 12:36.395
&lt;i>You want to have a little fun&lt;/i>

12:36.560 --> 12:37.675
&lt;i>You brush your teeth&lt;/i>

12:38.480 --> 12:40.118
What are you watching?

12:40.840 --> 12:42.193
The master at work.

12:42.360 --> 12:44.749
&lt;i>You wake up in the morning&lt;/i>
&lt;i>And it's quarter to 2

12:44.920 --> 12:48.515
&lt;i>You want to find something to do&lt;/i>
&lt;i>You brush your teeth&lt;/i>

12:50.800 --> 12:53.439
Oh, Raffi,
you magnificent son of a bitch.

12:55.800 --> 12:58.439
How do you do it?
How does he do it, Alan?

12:58.600 --> 12:59.919
What's he got that I don't?

13:00.520 --> 13:02.112
Well, based on first impressions...

13:02.280 --> 13:05.716
...I'd say, a genuine love of children,
and bladder control.

13:07.040 --> 13:10.191
- Well, that was just a cheap shot.
- I take them when I get them.

13:11.720 --> 13:15.030
Look at him. All relaxed and smiling.

13:15.480 --> 13:17.789
Last time I was
in front of an audience like that...

13:17.960 --> 13:19.393
...seventh-grade talent show...

13:19.560 --> 13:22.438
...I started shaking, sweating,
felt like I wanted to throw up.

13:22.600 --> 13:24.511
Don't forget peeing in your pants.

13:27.080 --> 13:28.832
You keep pitching me fat ones.

13:30.880 --> 13:32.871
- I'm not talking to you anymore.
- Oh, come on.

13:33.040 --> 13:35.998
Look, if you knew in the seventh grade
that you couldn't perform...

13:36.160 --> 13:37.832
...why'd you become a musician?

13:38.000 --> 13:41.037
Because there's one thing
I am more afraid of than an audience.

13:41.200 --> 13:42.758
What's that? An honest day's work?

13:44.400 --> 13:47.392
If you knew the answer,
why'd you ask the question?

13:52.040 --> 13:53.632
&lt;i>Charlie Waffles. Charlie Waffles.&lt;/i>

13:53.800 --> 13:55.119
Where the hell is he, Alan?

13:55.280 --> 13:58.272
I don't know. He said he wanted to
take a walk to calm himself down.

13:58.440 --> 14:00.635
I promise you,
I will crucify that son of a bitch.

14:00.800 --> 14:03.155
The two of you will be
in a box over a heating vent...

14:03.320 --> 14:04.912
...when I get through suing him.

14:05.480 --> 14:08.199
Could it be a box with a guest room?

14:08.880 --> 14:09.869
Hey, Alan.

14:10.480 --> 14:12.516
I figured out what went wrong
in seventh grade.

14:12.680 --> 14:13.715
What?

14:14.280 --> 14:16.669
I hadn't started drinking yet.

14:18.440 --> 14:21.955
- Charlie, you have to get out there.
- Right.

14:22.120 --> 14:23.872
The little bastards await.

14:27.280 --> 14:29.999
You can't sue him
if he just stinks, right?

14:36.920 --> 14:38.433
Who loves kids?

14:38.600 --> 14:41.114
Charlie Waffles.

14:41.280 --> 14:43.032
You're damn right.

15:09.560 --> 15:11.596
That one's not on the CD.

15:13.480 --> 15:14.993
Let's try this again.

15:18.720 --> 15:22.235
&lt;i>I drink from a sippy cup&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Sippy cup, sippy cup&lt;/i>

15:22.400 --> 15:25.073
&lt;i>I drink from a sippy cup&lt;/i>
&lt;i>'Cause I'm a big kid now&lt;/i>

15:25.240 --> 15:26.229
&lt;i>Come on&lt;/i>

15:26.400 --> 15:29.915
&lt;i>I drink from a sippy cup&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Sippy cup, sippy cup&lt;/i>

15:30.080 --> 15:33.436
&lt;i>I drink from a sippy cup&lt;/i>
&lt;i>'Cause I'm a big kid now&lt;/i>

15:33.600 --> 15:35.477
&lt;i>Bye-bye, boobies&lt;/i>

15:35.640 --> 15:37.312
